<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Spinola family</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Spinola were one of the great noble families of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genoa">Genoa</a>, rivals and at times allies of the Doria, Fieschi and Grimaldi. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oberto-spinola">Oberto Spinola</a> shared power with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oberto-doria">Oberto Doria</a> from 1270, and later Spinolas served as doges, bankers to the Spanish crown and generals. The best known, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ambrogio-spinola">Ambrogio Spinola</a>, commanded Spanish armies in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/low-countries">Low Countries</a> in the early 17th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/spinola-family.jpg" alt="Spinola family" width="320" height="372" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_the_house_of_Spinola.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
